le but the sting is taking off  that not only because he gets minimized  in terms of how it frequently appears  but because he's not around Batman and  he's not around characters who feel  obligated like they have to bond with  him cuz you know in Batman's case it's  his kid he's around characters who are  fine basically telling him to shut up  the villains are much better in this one  of the big ones is the heretic who again  is a character I don't know but I found  him interesting right off the bat in  terms of look and feel and vibe and then  once I found out more about him I found  him really intriguing as as a concept  and the way was being used  I think the villains stuff that happens  in the second half of the movie isn't  quite as good as sort of hits a peak as  we learn more about heretic and then  things good not bad but they get  oversimplified but the action stays good  so it's able to kind of steamroll over  that issue  Batwoman all wow Battlement first of all  her look her design gorgeous I love the  design of this character I love the way  she moves I love the way the hair moves  in that cape is awesome love it and  another great thing and not that this  had necessarily been a problem in new 52  based stories in particular but it is a  frequent issue with superhero stories  particularly dealing with younger  characters which is that whoever they're  trying to hide their secret identity  from this one has basically none of that  there's one toss off side thing with  that Dick Grayson as a girlfriend who  doesn't know but that's basically used  as a joke everyone else everybody knows  who everyone is there's no sidestepping  around like oh I can't let you know who  I am and this important person in my  life doesn't know everybody knows so  that BS is gone and we can just focus on  the stuff that works in the action and  the mystery behind what's going on and  the mystery is pretty good I mean it I  don't think it's a spoiler to say that  Batman is not d